1 0 0 1 54 450 Tm
(3. The Most Important Distinction) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 428 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 410 Tm
(People often confuse the model and the agent.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 392 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 374 Tm
(The model is not the whole agent.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 356 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 338 Tm
(The model reasons.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 320 Tm
(The agent manages.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 302 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 284 Tm
(That means:) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 266 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 248 Tm
(• the model interprets what the user wants) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 230 Tm
(• the agent turns that interpretation into a safe, executable workflow) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 212 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 194 Tm
(This is why the correct high-level flow is:) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 176 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 158 Tm
(User -> Frontend -> Backend -> Agent -> Model -> Agent -> MCP Server -> Tool -> Result) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 140 Tm
(-> Agent -> Model -> Agent -> Backend -> Frontend -> User) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 122 Tm
() Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 104 Tm
(This version is more accurate than placing the model before the agent as a separate) Tj
/F1 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 86 Tm
(top-level stage, because the model lives inside the agent loop.) Tj
